        "topic": "Timber Seasoning Methods & Defects",
        "question_text": "<p>What is the primary cause of <b>honeycombing</b> in seasoned timber?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p><i>Honeycombing</i> occurs when timber is dried too rapidly, causing internal checks (cracks) that resemble a honeycomb. This defect weakens the timber and reduces its structural integrity.</p>",
